# Root Prettier ignore (SHY-0448).
#
# lint-staged and CI both run Prettier from the repository root, and Prettier
# reads the ignore file next to its working directory. Until now there was none
# here, so `express-api/.prettierignore` — the only one in the tree — was never
# consulted from root. Its entries are carried over below so express-api's
# behaviour is unchanged, which SHY-0448 requires.
#
# That gap was not theoretical. `express-api/.prettierignore` protects
# `public/js/legal-translations.js` as "deliberately single-line per locale",
# and from the root Prettier wanted to reformat it anyway. Adding
# `prettier --check` over `public/` without this file would have destroyed the
# formatting somebody had already written down a reason for.

# ── Carried over from express-api/.prettierignore ──
node_modules/
coverage/
package-lock.json
test-results/

# ── Vendored and generated assets ──
# Not ours to format. Mirrors the `ignores` in public/eslint.config.mjs so the
# two tools agree about what is vendored.
**/*.min.js
**/vendor/**

# ── Locale tables: DATA, not code ──
#
# Every translation table under public/ is excluded, not just the compressed
# ones. Two independent reasons, and either alone is sufficient:
#
# 1. Several are written one line per locale ON PURPOSE. They are read by
#    comparing rows DOWN the file — one per language — so a missing or wrong
#    translation is visible at a glance across twenty of them. Expanding each
#    row into a block does not change the style, it removes the only way they
#    are reviewable. `express-api/.prettierignore` already said this about
#    legal-translations.js; the entry simply never took effect from the root.
#
# 2. 36 web specs assert locale COMPLETENESS by matching the shape of these
#    files — `zh: { ... }` blocks and the keys inside them. Re-serialising the
#    data would break those assertions, or worse, leave them passing while
#    matching something else. A formatter has no opinion worth that.
public/admin/translations.js
public/js/event-translations.js
public/js/homepage-translations.js
public/js/legal-translations.js
public/js/suggestions-i18n.js
public/portal/portal-translations.js
